### Structs in Rust

Structs let you group related values together:

```rust
struct User {
    username: String,
    active: bool,
    sign_in_count: u64,
}
```

#### Methods and Associated Functions
Methods are functions defined inside an `impl` block that take `&self`, `&mut self`, or `self` as their first argument:

```rust
struct Rectangle {
    width: u32,
    height: u32,
}

impl Rectangle {
    // Associated function (constructor) - called as Rectangle::new(...)
    pub fn new(width: u32, height: u32) -> Self {
        Self { width, height }
    }

    // Method - called on an instance as rect.area()
    pub fn area(&self) -> u32 {
        self.width * self.height
    }
}
```

